# fixedbugs, defect 171, lane ffimsg, 2026-10-03: why the binding is not
# refused. A loader's API is function pointers the loader sets at run time,
# volk naming each by the API's own name, `vkCreateInstance`, and GLAD
# naming it `glad_glClear` behind `#define glClear glad_glClear`; C calls
# them as functions, and so does this program, correctly. A `build` that
# refused a pointer bound as a function would refuse it, and every program
# over volk, GLAD or GLEW with it; measured, it builds and prints 5 and 9
# today.

extern "fixedbugs-171-a-loaders-pointers-set-then-called.h"
    function load_all()
    function vkAdd(a: i32, b: i32) -> i32
    function glAdd(a: i32, b: i32) -> i32

function main()
    load_all()
    print(vkAdd(a: 2, b: 3))
    print(glAdd(a: 4, b: 5))
